F-QS1: announce under a .local. host name, and report a refusal

The receiver's announcement never went out. build_service gave the
service its bare instance name as host name: that suited the mdns-sd
fork upstream used, but since 0.11.0 mdns-sd's `register()` refuses any
host name that does not end in ".local." (service_daemon.rs:539-541,
4712-4714), and patch 0007 moved to 0.21. `run()` called `register()?`
before its loop, so the task ended with an error at once; the embedding
application, which had spawned it, saw nothing, and no Android phone ever
listed the device as a receiver.

The host name is now `<instance>.local.`. The service is registered in
`MDnsServer::new`, so that a refusal is the caller's error to report
(Sukkula reports it as Quick Share failing to start); `run()` announces
until cancelled and says goodbye. A daemon whose setup fails part-way is
shut down instead of left running. `with_port` (hidden) makes either
daemon on another UDP port, for tests, which must not announce anything
on the network they run on.

tests/mdns.rs registers a service on loopback and a second mDNS daemon
resolves it: port, host name, address, and the endpoint info in the `n`
record, then the goodbye. Without the host-name fix, `new` fails with
"Hostname must end with '.local.'".

Findings: Sukkula review 2026-09-25 kept[0].
